15:["$","ul","b1787-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b1787",{"children":["Removal and replacement are separate problems: judge cutouts on hair and transparency, replacements on whether the light direction matches"]}],["$","li","b1789",{"children":["Masking isn't always right. To clear text or a small object, regenerating the frame with an instruction often beats drawing a mask."]}],["$","li","b1791",{"children":["Previews are downscaled almost everywhere, so check output resolution before you export"]}],["$","li","b1793",{"children":["If the cutout then needs four channel ratios, the tool that does both beats the marginally better cutout"]}]]}]
16:["$","h2","b1795",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-background-tool","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good background tool?"]}]
17:["$","p","b1797",{"children":["Four criteria, and the first one eliminates most tools for most professional work."]}]
18:["$","h3","b1799",{"children":["Edge quality on hard subjects"]}]
19:["$","p","b1801",{"children":["Every tool handles a clear-edged product. Hair against a busy background, a wine glass, a chain-link fence, motion blur: those separate them. Test your worst image, never your easiest."]}]
1a:["$","h3","b1803",{"children":["Light that matches"]}]
1b:["$","p","b1805",{"children":["The usual giveaway in a replaced background isn't a ragged cutout, it's a subject lit from the left dropped into a scene lit from the right. Either the tool relights the subject or it generates the scene from a description of the existing light."]}]
1c:["$","h3","b1807",{"children":["Volume that matches your volume"]}]
1d:["$","p","b1809",{"children":["A thousand pack shots and one hero image are opposite requirements. Per-image tools and batch pipelines are priced and shaped for one each, and using the wrong one is expensive in either direction."]}]
1e:["$","h3","b1811",{"children":["What happens next"]}]
1f:["$","p","b1813",{"children":["A cutout is rarely the deliverable. It gets composited, resized, branded and shipped. Count those steps when you compare, because a tool that hands back a transparent PNG has finished a third of the work."]}]
20:["$","h2","b1815",{"id":"the-five-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The five compared"]}]
21:["$","div","b1816",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b1817",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b18170",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b1820",{"children":[["$","strong","b1819",{"children":[""]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b18171",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b1823",{"children":[["$","strong","b1822",{"children":["Remove background"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b18172",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b1826",{"children":[["$","strong","b1825",{"children":["Replace background"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b18173",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b1829",{"children":[["$","strong","b1828",{"children":["Ease of starting"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b18174",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b1832",{"children":[["$","strong","b1831",{"children":["Next steps in the same tool"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b1833",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b18330",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1836",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b18331",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1839",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18332",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1842",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18333",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1845",{"children":["Describe it, no setup"]}]]}],["$","td","b18334",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1848",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b1849",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b18490",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1852",{"children":["Photoroom"]}]]}],["$","td","b18491",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1855",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18492",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1858",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18493",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1861",{"children":["One upload"]}]]}],["$","td","b18494",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1864",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b1865",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b18650",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1868",{"children":["Clipdrop"]}]]}],["$","td","b18651",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1871",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18652",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1874",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b18653",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1877",{"children":["One upload"]}]]}],["$","td","b18654",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1880",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}]]}],"$L59","$L5a"]}]}]}]
22:["$","h2","b1914",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
23:["$","p","b1916",{"children":["Melius, the Agentic OS for creative work, is a node-based creative canvas that AI agents operate alongside you. Background editing isn't a separate mode: every image node carries its own editing tools, so the edit happens where the image already lives."]}]
24:["$","p","b1918",{"children":["Melius has three built-in tools that cover most of the work. Remove Background outputs a transparent PNG. Inpaint lets you mask a region and describe what fills it, which is right when most of the frame must stay untouched. Upscale raises resolution afterward if you drafted low."]}]
25:["$","h3","b1920",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
26:["$","ul","b1922-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b1922",{"children":["Ships a Background Generator template for producing different backgrounds for a product, and Portrait Mode for a blurred-background look"]}],["$","li","b1924",{"children":["Handles the counter-intuitive case properly: to clear text from an image, regenerating the frame with an instruction to recreate it without the text usually beats masking, because a mask leaves you fighting the seam"]}],["$","li","b1926",{"children":["A cutout stays a node, so it feeds straight into a generated scene, picks up your logo as a separate reference, and runs through Magic Resize for every ratio you ship"]}],["$","li","b1931",{"children":["Model choice per step comes from ",["$","$L5b","b1929",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b1928","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false},"children":["one subscription"]}]," across the library of leading models, so the model that renders a convincing scene isn't a separate purchase from the one handling fine edges"]}]]}]
27:["$","p","b1933",{"children":["Two qualifiers. There's no dedicated relight control, so matching light means specifying it in the prompt or picking the model that handles it best, which is less direct than a slider. And a canvas is more tool than a single cutout needs: if you want one transparent PNG in ten seconds, opening a canvas is the slow route."]}]
28:["$","p","b1936",{"children":[["$","strong","b1934",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"background work that's one step inside a larger piece of creative, and teams who want the cutout, the new scene and the channel variants in one place."]}]
29:["$","h2","b1938",{"id":"2-photoroom","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Photoroom"]}]
2a:["$","p","b1940",{"children":["Photoroom is the volume answer, and background removal is one of its better use cases. Bulk background removal and batch editing are core, so a catalog goes through it as a queue."]}]
2b:["$","p","b1942",{"children":["Plans are metered in AI credits and monthly exports, which lets you size a plan against how many product images you actually process, and there's an API for teams putting it inside their own pipeline."]}]
2c:["$","h3","b1944",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2d:["$","ul","b1946-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b1946",{"children":["Bulk background removal, so a thousand pack shots is a job rather than a thousand jobs"]}],["$","li","b1948",{"children":["Batch editing across a set, holding the same treatment on every image"]}],["$","li","b1950",{"children":["Credit and export tiers you can match to real catalog volume"]}],["$","li","b1952",{"children":["An API for wiring it into an existing product pipeline"]}]]}]
2e:["$","p","b1954",{"children":["It aims squarely at product and listing imagery, and reviewers report its effectiveness is limited beyond that scope. If the job is one editorial image where the background has to be invented and art-directed, this is the wrong shape, and there is no canvas here for composing a scene from references."]}]
2f:["$","p","b1957",{"children":[["$","strong","b1955",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"catalogs, marketplace listings, and any case where the same background treatment is being run without a need for flexibility."]}]
30:["$","h2","b1959",{"id":"3-clipdrop","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Clipdrop"]}]
31:["$","p","b1961",{"children":["Clipdrop is an effective utility here, and its structure is why. It's eight separate tools, not a workflow: background removal, replace background, cleanup, uncrop, relight, text remover, upscale and text to image. You open the one you need and you're done."]}]
32:["$","p","b1963",{"children":["Relight deserves singling out, because mismatched lighting is the usual reason a replaced background looks wrong and few tools address it directly."]}]
33:["$","h3","b1965",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
34:["$","ul","b1967-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b1967",{"children":["Background removal and replace background as two distinct tools, so you pick the job"]}],["$","li","b1969",{"children":["Relight, which fixes the tell that gives most composites away"]}],["$","li","b1971",{"children":["Cleanup, uncrop and text remover for the small repairs a cutout usually needs"]}],["$","li","b1973",{"children":["A real free tier with a daily cap per tool, and a paid tier that raises both the cap and the upscale ceiling"]}]]}]
35:["$","p","b1975",{"children":["There's no brand memory and no batch, so it stays a per-image tool. That's fine for a handful of images and wrong for a catalog, and it means nothing you do in one session informs the next."]}]
36:["$","p","b1978",{"children":[["$","strong","b1976",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"single images and quick repairs."]}]
37:["$","h2","b1980",{"id":"4-flair","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Flair"]}]
38:["$","p","b1982",{"children":["Flair is the tactile option here. You stage a scene on a drag-and-drop canvas, arranging props around your product, then run an AI pass to finish it, which makes background composition something you position rather than something you describe."]}]
39:["$","h3","b1984",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3a:["$","ul","b1986-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b1986",{"children":["Digital scene staging with drag-and-drop props, so you control where things sit"]}],["$","li","b1988",{"children":["Background regeneration alongside general image editing"]}],["$","li","b1990",{"children":["On-model fashion photography with pattern preservation"]}],["$","li","b1992",{"children":["A custom AI human model builder, plus an API and team collaboration"]}]]}]
3b:["$","p","b1994",{"children":["Flair is built for e-commerce and it stays there. There's no video, audio or wider content pipeline in the same place, and no agent assembling the work, so you're doing the staging. For product backgrounds specifically that hands-on quality is a strength, and for a portrait or an editorial image it's the wrong shape."]}]
3c:["$","p","b1997",{"children":[["$","strong","b1995",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"e-commerce and fashion teams who want to do hands-on work arranging a product scene."]}]
3d:["$","h2","b1999",{"id":"5-comfyui","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. ComfyUI"]}]
3e:["$","p","b2001",{"children":["ComfyUI is the choice when nothing off the shelf does what you need. It's an open-source node-based interface where you build the pipeline yourself, so any masking, matting or compositing approach that exists can be assembled at the precision you want."]}]
3f:["$","h3","b2003",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
40:["$","ul","b2005-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2005",{"children":["Control over matting, masking and compositing"]}],["$","li","b2007",{"children":["Free and open source, with a desktop build for self-hosting and a managed cloud that has a free tier to start on"]}],["$","li","b2009",{"children":["Scriptable, so genuine batch processing is achievable"]}],["$","li","b2011",{"children":["A large community-built ecosystem of custom nodes and shareable workflows"]}]]}]
41:["$","p","b2013",{"children":["You pay in time and expertise. Setup, model management and debugging are yours, with no support line when a workflow breaks."]}]
42:["$","p","b2016",{"children":[["$","strong","b2014",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"technical users with a specific pipeline requirement no product covers."]}]
43:["$","h2","b2018",{"id":"editing-a-background-on-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Editing a background on Melius"]}]
44:["$","p","b2020",{"children":["Decide first whether you're removing or replacing, because they're different nodes. Remove Background returns a transparent PNG for a clean cutout. The Background Generator template builds a new scene around the subject, and the thing to watch there is light direction: a subject lit from one side dropped into a scene lit from the other is the tell."]}]
45:["$","p","b2025",{"children":["For a small object or stray text in the frame, the docs point the other way from instinct: regenerating the region with an instruction usually beats drawing a mask. Inpaint is for when most of the frame has to stay exactly as it is. Once the image is right, Magic Resize produces each channel ratio by re-composing rather than trimming, and the Studio node handles layered text on top. If you'd rather hand the whole sequence over, ",["$","$L5b","b2023",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2022","href":"/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","isNewTab":false},"children":["an agent can drive the canvas over MCP"]}]," and run the steps for you."]}]
46:["$","p","b2027",{"children":["Hair, glass and other semi-transparent edges remain the category's weak point. Test your hardest image before you commit to a pipeline."]}]
47:["$","p","b2032",{"children":["If the subject is a person rather than a product, the next decision is whether the portrait can stay recognizable and consistent across a team: see ",["$","$L5b","b2030",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2029","href":"/blog/turn-picture-into-professional-headshot-tools-ranked","isNewTab":false},"children":["tools to turn a picture into a professional headshot"]}],"."]}]
48:["$","p","b2037",{"children":["If the new background is meant to be painted rather than photographic, the tools that handle a painterly pass are a different set: see ",["$","$L5b","b2035",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2034","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting","isNewTab":false},"children":["the best AI tools to turn images into a painting"]}],"."]}]
49:["$","p","b2042",{"children":["If the background is one step inside a larger product job, the wider question is which tool holds the product itself steady across a set: see ",["$","$L5b","b2040",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2039","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","isNewTab":false},"children":["the best AI tools for producing product photo variants"]}],"."]}]
4a:["$","p","b2050",{"children":["Credits are shared across every model and every step, so a cutout, a generated scene and five channel ratios draw from the same balance. ",["$","$L5b","b2045",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2044","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},"children":["See pricing"]}],", or ",["$","$L5b","b2048",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2047","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["open Melius"]}]," and try it on one image."]}]
4b:["$","h2","b2052",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
4c:["$","div","b2053",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI photo background editing tool?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"It depends which of the two jobs you have. For background work that continues into a scene, brand assets and channel variants, Melius keeps those steps on one canvas. For a large catalog, Photoroom is built for that volume. For a single image or a lighting mismatch, Clipdrop. For staging a product scene by hand, Flair. And for a requirement no product covers, ComfyUI."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How do I replace a background so it looks real?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Match the light before the scene. The usual tell is a subject lit from one side dropped into a background lit from the other. Either generate the replacement from a description that specifies the existing light direction, or relight the subject to match. Perspective and horizon height give it away for the same reason."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Should I inpaint or regenerate the whole image?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Inpaint when most of the frame must stay exactly as it is and one region changes. Regenerate when the thing you want gone is spread across the frame, like text, because a full pass with an instruction to recreate the image without it leaves a cleaner result than a mask."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can AI remove a background from hair or glass?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":"$L5c"}]]}],"$L5d"]}],"$L5e","$L5f"]}]
4d:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L60","post-melius-summer-internship",{"post":{"_key":"post-melius-summer-internship","slug":"melius-summer-internship","category":"modus-news","title":"My Summer Internship with Melius","isoDate":"2026-08-19","date":"August 19, 2026","readTime":"7 Min Read","excerpt":"Wrapping up my summer engineering internship at Melius. Here is what I got to own, from building agent skills and context to the Playground, plus the team culture, the pre-launch off-site, and what I learned about product engineering and UX.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Nicholas Chen, Member of Technical Staff Intern"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is Melius?","answer":"Melius is an agents lab for creatives, marketing teams, and filmmakers. It gives you access to every major image and video model through a single interface, and Mel, its AI agent, handles the tedious work so you can generate whatever you imagine without leaving the app."},{"question":"What is the Playground in Melius?","answer":"The Playground is the fastest way to create in Melius: you describe what you want, pick a model and format, choose how many variations, and hit generate. Under the hood every Playground session is still a real canvas, so nothing you make is throwaway and you can open it in the full canvas whenever you want more control."},{"question":"What are agent skills and context in Melius?","answer":"Skills and context are two ways to give Mel instructions. Context is applied automatically on every turn, so it is where team conventions, brand guidelines, and preferences live. Skills are applied selectively when they are relevant to a task, and they can carry reference images alongside written instructions, which makes them useful for things like a product-photography look or keeping a character consistent."},{"question":"What was it like to intern at Melius?","answer":"Interning at Melius meant owning larger projects end to end and shipping directly to customers on a small team. Alongside the engineering there were team dinners and a lot of Super Smash Bros."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"starting-my-engineering-internship","title":"Starting My Engineering Internship"},{"_key":"agent-context-and-skills","title":"Agent Context and Skills"},{"_key":"the-playground","title":"The Playground"},{"_key":"work-hard-play-hard","title":"Work Hard, Play Hard"},{"_key":"key-takeaways","title":"Key Takeaways"},{"_key":"wrapping-up","title":"Wrapping Up"},{"_key":"faq","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1705","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1704","text":"Starting My Engineering Internship","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"starting-my-engineering-internship"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1707","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1706","text":"My internship at Melius has been an awesome learning experience for me as an engineer and a creative. Over the past few months, I had the opportunity to work on small and large projects that directly impacted our customers and also got to see the product scale and the team grow alongside it. I'm now wrapping up my last week and wanted to summarize everything I worked on, learned and enjoyed about Melius.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1709","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1708","text":"For context, Melius is an agents lab for creatives, marketing teams, and filmmakers to generate beautiful scenes and videos with access to image and video models through a single interface. Mel, our AI agent, does all the tedious work, so users are able to generate anything from their imagination without ever leaving the app.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1711","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1710","text":"In the past, I've worked at other startups and larger companies, but at Melius, what I loved most was being able to take on larger projects, have more ownership over the product, and wear many hats throughout the term.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1713","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1712","text":"Agent Context and Skills","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"agent-context-and-skills"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1715","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1714","text":"One of the larger projects I got to own was building out skills and context for our agent. The idea originally came up when we wanted Mel to follow certain instructions, but only during specific sessions. When we first started brainstorming solutions, we looked at how skills and context are typically used with AI agents. Both can essentially be represented as Markdown files containing instructions for the model, but the key difference is when they're applied. Context is applied automatically on every agent turn, while skills are selectively applied when they're relevant to a specific task.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1717","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1716","text":"Since Melius offers a creative canvas, we also wanted our skills to go beyond the typical Markdown file. A lot of creative direction is easier to show than describe, so we designed our skills to include reference images alongside written instructions. This opens up a bunch of useful workflows: a product photography skill could include instructions and references for a specific composition, while a character skill could help maintain consistency across generations. Context, on the other hand, could capture things that should always apply, like team conventions, brand guidelines, or other preferences Mel should know on every turn.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1718","caption":"How agent skills and context work together","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/agent-architecture.webp","alt":"How agent skills and context work together","aspectRatio":"2536 / 1504"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1720","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1719","text":"The goal of both features is ultimately to make prompting less repetitive. You tell Mel what you want to create, context gives it what it should already know, and your selected skills provide the task-specific instructions and references it needs. A big part of building this was also figuring out the product UX and making sure these features felt intuitive within the existing creative workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1722","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1721","text":"Working on this ended up being one of my favorite projects because it sat at the intersection of engineering, product, and creative tooling. I got to think through the agent architecture, build the underlying system, and figure out how to make it feel intuitive inside a creative workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1725","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b1723","href":"https://x.com/trymelius/status/2066941446247108899?s=20","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1724","text":"Here's a demo of the feature","marks":["b1723"]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1726","caption":"Agent skills and context in the Melius app settings","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/agent-skills-settings.webp","alt":"Agent skills and context in the Melius app settings","aspectRatio":"1974 / 906"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1728","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1727","text":"The Playground","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-playground"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1730","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1729","text":"Another fun project I got to work on was the Playground. Before this, Melius started off as a creative canvas where users could create generation workflows together, make edits, and build out entire scenes in an infinite space. But not every creative task needs a full canvas, so we wanted to give users a faster way to simply type a prompt and start creating.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1732","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1731","text":"The Playground is a simpler, more intuitive way to create: you describe what you want, pick a model and format, choose how many variations, and hit generate. The Playground mirrored the canvas experience, making it easy for existing Melius users to bring over their work while still being approachable for new users. All the generations in the Playground are saved to each user's personal history within their team, making it easy to revisit their work later.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1734","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1733","text":"What I like most about how we built it is that under the hood, every Playground session is still a real canvas. Nothing you make is throwaway so the moment you want more control, you can open it in the full canvas and keep working with all of Mel's tools. That let the Playground lower the barrier to entry without cutting anyone off from the depth underneath.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1735","caption":"The playground architecture under the hood","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/playground-architecture.webp","alt":"The playground architecture under the hood","aspectRatio":"2000 / 412"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1737","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1736","text":"This was another project that made me think hard about UX. The whole point was to remove friction for people who might be intimidated by a blank canvas, so a lot of the work came down to small product decisions: what information to show upfront, what to hide until it was needed, how users selected models and formats, and how we could make the path from an idea to a generation as simple as possible. At the same time, we wanted the Playground to fit naturally into the rest of Melius, so users could start with something simple and move into the canvas when they needed more control or more advanced workflows. (Shoutout to Winson for the designs!)","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1739","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1738","text":"This was probably the most fun project I got to work on during my internship, and I was really happy with how it turned out. Seeing so many users using the Playground after we shipped it was especially rewarding and made all the small product and UX decisions feel worth it. Lots of learning came out of this and I couldn't have done it without Ray, who helped get it to the finish line.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1742","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b1740","href":"https://x.com/trymelius/status/2080757663139520622?s=20","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1741","text":"Showcase of the Playground in Melius","marks":["b1740"]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1743","caption":"An example image generated in the Playground","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/playground-showcase.webp","alt":"Showcase of the Playground in Melius","aspectRatio":"2000 / 1339"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1745","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1744","text":"Work Hard, Play Hard","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"work-hard-play-hard"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1747","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1746","text":"Of course, the internship wasn't all work. Some of my favorite memories at Melius came from the things we did together outside of our usual day-to-day. We had team dinners, did yoga together, and generally spent a lot of time getting to know each other beyond work. Most of our days ended with playing a few games of Super Smash Bros.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1748","caption":"The Melius team doing yoga at 8am in the morning","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/team-yoga.webp","alt":"The Melius team doing yoga at 8am in the morning","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1750","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1749","text":"One of the highlights was our team off-site in upstate New York leading up to launch. We spent three or four days together in a huge house, basically living and working under the same roof. We were revamping major parts of the app, fixing things that hadn't mattered as much at a smaller scale, and making sure the product and infrastructure was ready for a much larger wave of users. Everyone was jumping between whatever needed to get done, and it was really cool getting to experience that side of building and launching a product firsthand. The off-site brought us closer as a team and made the internship that much more memorable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1755","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b1752","href":"https://x.com/n0w00j/status/2075594907285139867?s=20","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1751","text":"After all the prep, seeing Melius finally launch was really cool! Check out the launch ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1753","text":"here","marks":["b1752"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1754","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"imageCompare","_key":"b1756","caption":"The team working on the app pre-launch during dinner at the offsite","images":[{"label":"","src":"/images/blog/melius-summer-internship/offsite-dinner.webp","alt":"The team working on the app pre-launch during dinner at the offsite","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1758","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1757","text":"Key Takeaways","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"key-takeaways"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1760","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1759","text":"My two biggest takeaways from being on the engineering team here at Melius were developing a stronger product engineering mindset and improving my communication skills.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1763","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1761","text":"Think Like a Product Engineer","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1762","text":" â€“ On the product side, I learned to think beyond whether something simply works and focus more on how it actually feels to use. At Melius, this was especially important since we're building for prosumers, many of whom aren't technical, so features like agents and generative models need to feel intuitive and approachable. This taught me to hold a much higher bar for UX when shipping customer-facing features and to care about the small details that shape the overall experience.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1766","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1764","text":"Communicate Clearly","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1765","text":" â€“ I also learned that communication is a huge part of being an effective engineer. Whether it's discussing technical decisions with other engineers or explaining ideas to non-engineers, being able to communicate clearly and efficiently keeps everyone aligned and allows the team to move faster.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1768","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1767","text":"Wrapping Up","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"wrapping-up"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1770","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1769","text":"Overall, I'm incredibly grateful for everything I got to experience. I came into the internship hoping to grow as an engineer, but I'm leaving with a much better understanding of what it means to build a product end-to-end. From owning larger projects, to thinking deeply about UX, and working across different parts of the stack, I was constantly learning something new.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1772","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1771","text":"What made the experience especially memorable was the amount of ownership and trust I was given. Being on a small team meant I got to work on things that shipped directly to customers and see the impact of what I was building. More than anything, I'm grateful for the people I got to work with while building something I genuinely enjoyed working on.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1774","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1773","text":"I'm excited to take everything I learned at Melius with me into whatever I build next! A huge thank you to Young, Joowon, Arnav, Ray, Jahow, Alex, Winson, Samantha and Max for making these past few months such a memorable experience.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1776","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1775","text":"FAQ","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"faq"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b1777","items":"$4d:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"}]}}],"$L61","$L62"]}]]}]]}]
